From: u63023c771a070260 at groups.google.com (Antonio Piccolboni)
Date: Mon, 23 Jul 2012 21:15:44 +0000
Subject: rmr 1.3 available
Message-ID: <u_N7fD7H5o8.QUdGyGqTVP8J@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/u_N7fD7H5o8/m/QUdGyGqTVP8J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rmr 1.3 offers:
An optional vectorized API for efficient R programming when dealing with small records.
Fast C implementations for serialization and deserialization from and to typedbytes.
Other readers and writers work much better in vectorized mode, namely csv and text
Additional steps to support structured data better, that is you can use more data frames and less lists in the API
More forgiving behavior for package loading and bug fixes
More details here: New in this release <http://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/4efbd435aff3d52cfea116b663100baf637035cc/rmr/pkg/docs/new-in-this-release.md>
Code speaks: rmr_1.3.tar.gz <https://github.com/downloads/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/rmr_1.3.tar.gz>
Introduction to the vectorized API <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/master/rmr/pkg/docs/introduction-to-vectorized-API.md>

We've made an effort to upgrade and reorganize the documentation around a new process whereby code-heavy documentation is versioned and tested just like the library itself, thanks to RStudio and knitr, but this process will be complete with the next minor. Enjoy and don't hold back your feedback.

Antonio

